> it really has helped me get a better grasp on some of the grammar. `to` And
> get pretty damn well confused about those mekso operators! `xau to` ;-)
>
> Could you please put the translation of your examples to "normal" Lojban
>> so that we can compare them?
>> I'm interested in your proposal.
>>
>>
> Done. I added two more examples too, but it's hard to find good examples
> b/c the terminators are so often elidable. If you have some better examples
> to replace the ones I have dug up that would be great.
>


Indeed, I never use {ku'o}. It seems like it is always elidable or
replaceable with {vau}.

As for other terminators. {be'o}  is necessary in {be'o poi} however, if
{poi poi} is allowed in the grammar then {be'o} can be dropped too.

{do'u} is often elidable if you say {COI do}/{doi do}.
{kei} is to be replaced with {vau}.
TEI and mekso are poorly thought out parts of the grammar so i won't even
comment.

I made a pull request fixing some mistypes.


